WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.579
More on that at the end. Arteries generally carry blood “away” from the heart.

00:00:05.629 --> 00:00:06.950
Think “A” for away.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.028
Arteries are typically oxygen-rich but there are exceptions.

00:00:11.078 --> 00:00:13.950
Veins generally carry blood “to” the heart.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.950
Veins typically are oxygen-poor but there are exceptions.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.507
Capillaries are small blood vessels and it is at the capillary level where oxygen is delivered to

00:00:23.557 --> 00:00:28.950
organs and tissues and where carbon dioxide will also be picked up to travel back to the lungs.
